x with `crypto.timingSafeEqual` on equal-length hashes of both values.\n\n**5. Minor issues**\n- The 401 response has no `WWW-Authenticate` header.\n- There is no failed-auth rate limiting. The README puts ingress policy under the host.\n- The session lookup is copied into two handlers. Pull it into a helper so the fix for item 1 lives in one place.\n- `GATEWAY_KEY` is read once at registration. That is fine, but rotating the key needs a restart.\n\n## Out of scope\nThe README assigns these to the host, so I didn't assess them:\n- `createTransport` internals\n- the secret store\n- audit logging\n- framing limits\n- process supervision\n\nSession IDs are random UUIDs and are only correlation handles behind the auth gate, so I don't count their guessability as an issue.","ttft_ms":1482,"type":"result","duration_ms":24870,"uuid":"88ae6dfc-10d9-410e-bc7d-5bf494778ea0","ttft_stream_ms":1182,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1183,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":6,"outputTokens":2680,"cacheReadInputTokens":14807,"cacheCreationInputTokens":2229,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.037208700000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":887,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
